---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Terms of Service" description="Terms of service for Sextant." path="/terms">
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="label-caps text-signal">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="display-type mt-3 text-4xl font-medium text-ink sm:text-5xl">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-3">Last updated: November 14, 2026</p>
    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">The service</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Sextant is an open-source template for building SaaS applications. The hosted instance is
          a demonstration. The template itself is provided under the MIT license.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Accounts</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You must provide accurate information when creating an account. You are responsible for
          keeping your credentials secure. You can delete your account at any time.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Payments</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The hosted instance uses Stripe in test mode. No real charges are made. If you deploy your
          own instance, you are responsible for your own payment configuration and compliance.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Acceptable use</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Do not use the service to spam, abuse the API, or violate any laws. We may suspend
          accounts that abuse the service.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The software is provided "as is" without warranty. We are not liable for any damages
          arising from its use.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
